# Chatwoot files the overlay stands in for, at the pinned tag (CHATWOOT_VERSION).
# The overlay never edits a file of Chatwoot. Where it needs one to behave
# differently, it supplies its own file and scripts/assemble.sh puts that in
# use. Each line:
#
#   <blob id> <Chatwoot path>              shims/<path> takes the file's place;
#                                          Chatwoot's own stays beside it, byte
#                                          for byte, as <name>.chatwoot.<ext>
#   <blob id> <Chatwoot path> <our file>   the Chatwoot file stays where it is;
#                                          <our file> is used instead of it (a
#                                          view found first, a component mounted)
#
# The blob id is the file's at the pinned tag (git rev-parse <tag>:<path>).
# assemble.sh stops when it no longer matches: Chatwoot changed the file, so
# read their change, carry over what our file needs, record the new id.

